THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC FOR ONE REASON

The forward archive inside index.html records what the model predicted before
the races it describes. The commit dates on those entries are the evidence,
and evidence nobody can inspect is not evidence. That is why this is readable.

Being able to read this work is not permission to use it. No licence is
granted by implication, and none is granted by the fact that the site serves
its complete source to every browser. Chute is one static file with no
backend; handing you the source is a consequence of how it is built, not an
offer of the code.

YOU MAY

  - read the source, the notes and the commit history
  - use the published site as a visitor
  - quote short excerpts, with attribution, for comment, criticism or review

YOU MAY NOT, without written permission

  - copy, mirror, republish or redistribute this repository or the served
    page, in whole or in substantial part
  - create derivative works, including a version adapted to another state,
    another sport, or another set of classifications
  - use any of it commercially
  - redistribute the compiled databases: the seed in index.html, the season
    data in backtest/data/, or the roster archives in pull/roster/

ON THE DATA

Race results are facts and belong to nobody. What is claimed here is the
compilation: the selection, correction and arrangement of those facts, which
is most of the work in this repository and none of it obvious. Deciding that a
junior varsity race is not a varsity one, that a July camp time trial is not
the season, that a relay split is not an open 400, and that two athlete
profiles are one person, is editorial judgement rather than transcription.

Marks and results are derived from athletic.net and from OSAA, and remain
subject to whatever terms those sources impose. Nothing here grants any right
in their data.

